"""
Anti-heeling tank.

Ported from `ShipSIM.Components.AntiHeelingSystem.Tank`.

The tank receives an input vector `[M_input, Q]` (heeling moment seen by the ship and the
pump flow rate in m³/h) and integrates a fill volume bounded by [0.05·V, 0.85·V]. The
sign of the heeling moment together with the sign of `CoG_trans` selects whether the pump
fills (positive direction) or empties (negative direction) the tank.

Differences from upstream:
- The Modelica original uses a single `RealInput[2]` for `(M_input, Q)`. Dyad doesn't
  support array-typed connectors as cleanly, so this version takes them as two separate
  scalar inputs.
- The hard-clip of `inter_volume` to `[0.05·V, 0.85·V]` is preserved verbatim using
  `clamp` (Dyad has no `if/elseif` cascade for an algebraic equation; `clamp` plays the
  same role).
- `der_m_esc` (derivative of moment input) is calculated but not used downstream, just as
  in the original. We drop it.
- The fill direction is reversed relative to upstream: a positive heeling moment
  (starboard down) fills the tank on the positive-`CoG_trans` (port) side, which is the
  side `AntiHeeling` moves ballast to when it produces its righting moment. Upstream
  drains that tank, contradicting its own moment.
"""
component Tank
  "Transversal position of CoG of tank (sign indicates port/starboard)"
  parameter CoG_trans::Length = 8.77
  "Tank volume capacity [m³]"
  parameter V::Real = 211.47
  "Tank height [m]"
  parameter H::Length = 5
  "Liquid density [t/m³] (Modelica original convention)"
  parameter rho::Real = 1.025
  "Initial fill fraction (0..1)"
  parameter initial_fill_fraction::Real = 0.45

  M_input = RealInput()         # heeling moment seen by ship [t·m]
  Q_input = RealInput()         # pump flow rate [m³/h]

  Q = RealOutput()              # pass-through of Q_input
  fill_level = RealOutput()     # 0..100
  volume = RealOutput()         # m³ in tank, after clamp
  tank_pressure = RealOutput()  # bar at lowest point

  variable inter_volume::Real
  variable indi_pos::Real
  variable indi_moment::Real
relations
  initial inter_volume = initial_fill_fraction * V

  Q = Q_input

  indi_pos = ifelse(CoG_trans < 0, -1, 1)
  indi_moment = ifelse(M_input > 0, 1, -1)

  der(inter_volume) = indi_pos * indi_moment * Q / 3600

  volume = clamp(inter_volume, 0.05 * V, 0.85 * V)
  fill_level = volume / V * 100
  tank_pressure = volume / V * H * rho * 9.81 / 100
end
